    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "3. Conditional distributions associated with the MVN are also multivariate normal. Consider the partitioning of x into two components, an $ (m \\times 1) $ column vector $ x_1 $ and an $ [(n-m) \\times 1] $ column vector $ x_2 $ of the remaining variables, e.g.,",
      "source_page": 212,
      "printed_page": 192,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p212:b9"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        155.0,
        461.0,
